JACobian ELIPPITIC FUNCTIONS AND THETA FUNCTIONS (p.16.4. Calculation of the Jacobian Functions by Use of the Arithmetic-Geometric Mean (A.G.M.)
For the A.G.M. scale see 17.6.
To calculate sn (u|m), cn (u|m), and dn (u|m) form the A.G.M. scale starting with
16.4.1   a_0=1, b_0=\sqrt{m}, c_0=\sqrt{m}, terminating at the step N when c_N is negligible to the accuracy required. Find p_N in degrees where
16.4.2  \varphi_N=2^Na_{N}u\frac{180^{n}}{\pi}\]
16.5. Special Arguments and then compute successively \varphi_N-1, \varphi_N-2, \varphi_1, \varphi_0 from the recurrence relation
16.4.3  \sin (2\varphi_{n-1}-\varphi_n)=\frac{c_n}{a_n}\sin\varphi_n.
Then
16.4.4  \sin (u|m)=\sin\varphi_b, cn (u|m)=\cos\varphi_0
dn (u|m)=\frac{\cos\varphi_0}{\cos\left(\varphi_1-\varphi_0\right)}. From these all the other functions can be determined.
